{"parentUuid":"0ba9b56b-7855-4ce2-8706-029ea4aeb638","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-17","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/print-bleed","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01q03MIWXyy6wpxNf90UcDRj","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PDF's pages are exactly A4 and every box equals the MediaBox; pdfinfo shows BleedBox and TrimBox only because they default to the CropBox. That is fine on screen, but not for print. A printer prints on bigger sheets and cuts them down to the trim size, and the cut can wander by a millimetre or so. Anything that should run to the edge, like our background colour, therefore has to extend past the cut line, the bleed, usually 3 mm on each side, and the PDF has to say where the cut line is with a TrimBox inside a larger MediaBox. Our backgrounds stop exactly at the page edge, so any drift of the blade shows white paper. Let me look at how pages are set up."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":757,"output_tokens":177}},"uuid":"3a53b762-8020-4f6a-93d0-800e0e0b90d8","timestamp":"2026-09-29T08:44:24.000Z","requestId":"req_011C23uHAjduBWpIuLuQ6lLl"}
